Then comes critical moment—at point marked "[DAY1 11:35:xx]" wherein two individuals speak simultaneously—one calling attention to tool availability ('scissors') whereas second confirms existence/location thereof (**"the scissors ARE here."**) 

Now recall original prompt asked WHO Originally Used Them ?

Key insight emerges if analyzing chronology properly—not merely listening order nor surface-level dialogues—to determine temporal precedence concerning actuation/use events surrounding said instrument(s). Specifically observe following progression below:

• First instance mentioning scissor reference = Alice stating 'Scissors.'  
→ Implies awareness/existence/naming event initiated solely by HER 
